    },
    {
      "title": "Infinite Primes",
      "pages": [3, 4],
      "text": "Euclid's proof demonstrates that there are infinitely many prime numbers. The proof involves multiplying all primes together and adding one, showing that the resulting number has a prime factor that was not included in the original list. Euler's proof further strengthens this by showing that the sum of the reciprocals of primes grows without limit."
    },
