      "pages": [8, 9],
      "text": "The document describes Euler's product, a formula connecting prime numbers to the sum of all whole numbers. It explains how this product represents the zeta function, which is fundamental to understanding prime distribution. Euler used this product to prove the infinitude of primes and to solve the Basel problem."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Basel Problem",
      "pages": [9],
      "text": "The Basel problem concerned the calculation of the sum of the reciprocals of the squares of all positive integers. Euler correctly determined that this sum equals pi squared divided by six, a surprising result that highlighted the connection between arithmetic and geometry."
